      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you need to return a value ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 415,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 415,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e397497_fa524f32",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/audio_util/MediaPlayerList.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 415,
      "author": {
        "id": 1880948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:56:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The return value corresponds to the addressed player after this method call. If it was set successfully then it returns the new addressed player, otherwise it\u0027ll return the previous one.\nAs for why, this is how the logic is implemented in the native (see device.cc), and changing this would be a pain with flags.",
      "parentUuid": "040fe6bb_af0ef486",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 415,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 415,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa36d937_d67b4354",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/audio_util/MediaPlayerList.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if it doesn\u0027t contains the value, should you return an error ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b1a2634_0c59b027",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/audio_util/MediaPlayerList.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1880948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:56:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the case already, if the addressed player returned is the previous one then we consider the event failed and we\u0027ll respond with `INVALID_PLAYER_ID`.",
      "parentUuid": "fa36d937_d67b4354",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29806bb1_47a07e97",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/audio_util/MediaPlayerList.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there is no addressed player, should it fall back to the active player ?\n\nShould all of this be \"getCurrentPlayer\" ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97d844e5_73f0cd19",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/audio_util/MediaPlayerList.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 595,
      "author": {
        "id": 1880948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-08T20:56:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Addressed player is linked to active player. Change in active player will be made in addressed player too, and calling SetAddressedPlayer will never result in \"no addressed player\". So if there is no addressed player, then there is no active player either.\n\nGetCurrentPlayerId doesn\u0027t return a MediaPlayerWrapper but an ID and should not be used when communicating with Android MediaSessions.",
      "parentUuid": "29806bb1_47a07e97",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 595,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 595,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "7f4d35d234053358b9f3711dd7216e6b81b1cd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
